Page 90 Anishinaabe: -------- begin text --------

===Noun===
{{oj-noun|l|g=an|pl=Anishinaabeg}}

# {{alt case|oj|anishinaabe}}
-------- end text --------
Page 91 anishinaabe: -------- begin text --------
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|oj|Anishinaabe}}
* {{l|oj|Nishnaabe}}
* {{l|oj|Nishnawbe}}

===Etymology===
There are many differing interpretations of Anishinaabe, but it is widely accepted that "-naabe", means "a male, a male of a species", or more generally "a person" . Anishinaabe is a [[cognate]] to the [[Oji-cree]] [[autonym]] ''"Anishinini"'' (''"inini"'' meaning man in both Oji-cree and Ojibwe)
Some suggested meanings of Anishinaabe:
* [[an(i)-]] "away" + [[niisin]] "lower somebody" + [[naabe]] "a male, a male of a species", meaning "man who was lowered (from the sky)".<ref>Oshkaabewis Native Journal (Vol. 2, No. 1)</ref><ref>http://ojibwe.lib.umn.edu/main-entry/niisin-vta</ref>
* [[anishinaa]] "first, original" + [[naabe]] "a male, a male of a species", meaning "first people" or "original people".

===Noun===
{{oj-noun|l|ᐊᓂᔑᓈᐯ|g=an|pl=anishinaabeg|dim=anishinaabens}}

# an [[Anishinaabe]] {{gloss|an [[Ojibwe]], [[Nipissing]], [[Algonquin]], [[Potawatomi]], or [[Odawa]]}}
## {{lb|oj|specifically}} an Ojibwe
##: {{syn|oj|ojibwe}}
# an [[Indian]], a [[Native]] {{q|especially one of North America|in contrast to a non-Native}}
#: {{ux|oj|Besho omaa daawag igi '''anishinaabeg'''.|The '''Natives''' live close by.}}
#* {{quote-book|oj|year=2014|author=George Kenny|title=Gaawiin Mawisiiwag Anishinaabeg: Indians Don't Cry|page=7
|passage=Gaawiin iindog [[mawi|mawisiiwag]] '''anishinaabeg'''. Gaawiin debwe iwe, inendam Frank Littledeer e-mamawid.|translation='''Indians''' don't cry. That's bullshit, Frank Littledeer cursed as tears streamed down his broad, weather-scarred face.}}
# a [[person]], a [[human]] {{q|in contrast to a non-human being}}

====Hyponyms====
