===Alternative forms===
* {{l|oj|idash}}
* {{l|oj|-sh}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|oj|/ˈdaʃ/}}

===Adverb===
{{head|oj|adverb|cat2=conjunctive adverbs}}

# and, and then, then
#: {{ux|oj|Bijiinag ninga-ozhi'aa a'aw bakwezhigan. Mii '''dash''' onadinag.|I'll make the bread later and '''then''' knead it.}}
# but

====Usage notes====
'''''dash''''' comes in the second position in a clause, indicating that one thing happened after another. It can also have a contrastive meaning and then may be translated with ''but.''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|oj|aaniin dash|t=why?}}
* {{l|oj|mii dash|t=and then}}

====See also====
