Page 623 izhi: -------- begin text --------

===Verb===
{{head|oj|verb|cat2=verb transitive animate (vta)}}

# say
#: {{ux|oj|'''Izhi''' ji-giiwed.|Tell him to go home.}}
# speak so

====Conjugation====
'''izhi''' is one of the few irregular verbs in Ojibwe. Generally speaking, ''{{l|oj|iN-}}'' is the stem onto which inflections are added. For example: ''od'''in'''aan - s/he says to him/her.'' The full conjugation can be found [https://web.archive.org/web/20080522022027/http://imp.lss.wisc.edu/~jrvalent/ais301/Grammar/HTMLParadigms/vtaIZHIindpos.htm here]

