#: {{usex|oj|Mii 'i gii-oshki-'''manoominikeyaang''' dagwaagong.|We went '''ricing''' for the first time last fall.}}
#: {{usex|oj|Ogii-pawaanaan '''manoominikenid''' oosan.|He dreamed about his father '''ricing'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|oj|author=Nancy Thompson|year=1983|title=Manoominikewin|text=Mewinzha e-gii-manoominikeyaang, gaawin wiikaa ngii-ani-izhi-maajii-manoominikesiimin: akawe e-gii-nanaakodamowaad gichi-anishnaabeg ji-bwaa-maajii-manoominikeng.|t=Long ago when we riced, we never just casually started ricing: always the elders gave thanks before we started ricing.|url=https://ojibwegrammar.langsci.wisc.edu/Stories/manoominikewin.html}}<!--This is part of a text provided by https://ojibwegrammar.langsci.wisc.edu/Stories/Stories.html as audio and as a text version but I don't know the best template to use. Also if anyone knows Nancy Thompson's Ojibwe name, please add it right before her English name-->

