Page 861 ni-: -------- begin text --------

===Prefix===
{{head|oj|prefix|cat2=personal prefixes}}

# {{non-gloss|A prefix denoting the first person}}

====Usage notes====
'''ni-''' is the unmarked form, and appears before stems that begin with the consonants p, t, k, h, ch, m, n, s, sh, w, and y. In animate intransitive verbs (vai) and transitive inanimate verbs (vti) conjugations, '''ni-''' or one of its alternative forms can act as part of a pair of affixes, with the affix {{l|oj|-min}} (or a variant) to form the first person plural exclusive . In transitive animate verbs (vta) - that is verbs where the subject and the object are both animate - '''ni-''' can indicate that either the subject or the object is first-person (singular or plural), according to the rules of topicality hierarchy.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|oj|im-}}
* {{l|oj|in-}}
* {{l|oj|ind-}}
* {{l|oj|indo-}}
* {{l|oj|n-}}
* {{l|oj|nim-}}
* {{l|oj|nin-}}
* {{l|oj|nind-}}
* {{l|oj|nindo-}}
* {{l|oj|niy-}}
* {{l|oj|nd-}}
* {{l|oj|ndo-}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|oj|niin}}
* {{l|oj|niinawind}}

====See also====
{{oj-personal prefixes}}

===Preverb===
{{head|oj|preverb|cat2=directional preverbs}}

# {{alternative spelling of|oj|ani-}}

