Page 916 niijii: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|oj|niij}}
* {{l|oj|niiji}}

===Etymology===
A vocative form perhaps derived from {{l|oj|niijikiwenh}} ''(my brother)''

===Noun===
{{head|oj|noun|cat2=animate nouns}}

# my friend
#: {{ux|oj|Boozhoo '''niijii'''.|Hello, my friend.}}
# a [[Native American]]

====Usage notes====
'''niijii''' is a form of direct address (vocative) traditionally used by men talking to each other.

It is also proposed by Native activists as a replacement for the terms "Indian" and "Native American". '''niijii''' can be used by any Native person to refer to themselves or their people, regardless of origin.

====See also====
* {{l|oj|niikaan}}

===References===
* The Ojibwe People's Dictionary https://ojibwe.lib.umn.edu/main-entry/main-entry/niijii-nad
