===Pronoun===
{{head|oj|pronoun|g=an|cat2=personal pronouns|Syllabics:|ᓃᓐ}}

# first-person singular pronoun: [[I]], [[me]]
#: {{ux|oj|Gegaa gii-pizikawaa anishaa go '''niin''' gaa-ikowebinag.|She would have been almost run over if it hadn't been for '''me''' pushing her out of the way.}}

====Usage notes====
Unlike in English, the first person is often expressed in Ojibwe by adding the personal prefix ''{{l|oj|ni-}}'' and a corresponding suffix to the verb. The indepedent personal pronoun '''niin''' is often used to express emphasis or contrast, or when there is no verb in the sentence.

====Related terms====
* {{l|oj|niinawind}}
* {{l|oj|niineta}}
* {{l|oj|niinitam}}
* {{l|oj|ni-}}

====See also====
{{oj-personal pronouns}}

===References===
* {{R:oj:OPD}}
-------- end text --------
